# ============================================================================
# MUAD'DIB .gitignore
# Reconstituted 2026-04-11 after merge commit e8db15e accidentally emptied it.
# Combines entries from 72626b8 (pre-merge) + post-audit additions (v2.10.74).
# ============================================================================

# --- Dependencies (node_modules must never be committed) ---
# Slash-less on purpose: a trailing-slash pattern is directory-only and does NOT
# ignore a *symlink* named node_modules. A stray `git add` of a self-referential
# node_modules symlink (ELOOP) got re-tracked once (commit 07d45dc8) precisely
# because `node_modules/` did not match it. Slash-less covers dir AND symlink.
node_modules

# --- Environment & secrets (SECURITY: never commit) ---
.env
.env.*
# Exception: .env.example is the documented template (no real values).
!.env.example

# --- Build artifacts & output files ---
*.tgz
*.vsix
package/
.nyc_output/
coverage/
metrics/
rapport.html
results.sarif

# --- Logs (with exception for one test fixture) ---
*.log
!tests/samples/gvisor/strace-sample.log

# --- Cache directories ---
.muaddib-cache/
.claude/

# --- IOC data (large files, downloaded via `npm run update`) ---
# src/ioc/data/iocs.json is 112 MB, iocs-compact.json is committed as a
# separate ~5 MB file at the root. The large downloaded version stays local.
src/ioc/data/
iocs-compact.json
iocs.json.gz
nul

# --- Local data files (large per-environment artifacts) ---
# Covers data/auto-labels.json (101 MB), data/ml-training-*.jsonl, data/tarball-cache/,
# data/daily-stats.json, data/detections.json, etc. Uses leading slash to restrict
# the pattern to the top-level data/ directory only (src/ioc/data/ has its own rule).
/data/

# --- Datasets (training corpora, benchmark results) ---
# Covers datasets/adversarial/, datasets/real-world/*.json, datasets/benign/, etc.
/datasets/

# --- ML retrain artifacts (training dumps — but auto-labeler Python code is tracked) ---
ml-retrain/retrain-dataset.jsonl
ml-retrain/*.jsonl
ml-retrain/tarballs/

# --- Monitor runtime artifacts ---
# logs/ contains alert files and webhook buffers — production state, never committed.
/logs/
/backups/

# --- Evaluation & session outputs (per-run local files) ---
tmp-*
evaluate-*.json
evaluate-*.txt
v267.txt
v268.txt
SESSION-LOG.md

# --- Audit bypass samples (SECURITY: evasion techniques must not be public) ---
# These samples demonstrate how an attacker would evade detection — publishing
# them would hand a recipe to adversaries.
tests/samples/audit-v3-bypasses/

# --- Review queue artifacts (v2.10.74 forensic audit) ---
# Contains tarballs + dumps from the VPS audit. May contain package contents
# from third parties — keep local only.
review-queue-export.tar.gz
review-queue/

# --- Local-only scripts (project pro dossier generator, throwaway helpers) ---
.build_dossier.py

# --- Local work artifacts (SECURITY + hygiene: keep `git add -A` safe) ---
# Added 2026-07-11: dozens of per-session working dirs, patches, audit dumps and
# snapshots were untracked, making a blind `git add -A` liable to sweep in gigabytes
# of scan data (archive/) or half-finished patches. All local-only scratch.
.venv/
archive/
.adjwork/
.muaddib/
.npm/
.sec-review-*/
.suite-data-snapshot/
*.patch

# --- Ephemeral dated reports / audit dumps / batch-scripts (throwaway) ---
# ROOT-ANCHORED (leading /) on purpose: a bare `audit-*` / `security-review-*` would
# shadow TRACKED paths (tests/audit-2026-05/, scripts/audit-archive.sh, the audit-*.test.js
# suites) and hide any new file added under them. Anchoring restricts to the root-level
# scratch. Kept trackable on purpose: analysis tooling (scripts/ml-*, ghsa-*, build-*),
# the remediation spec, ml-retrain/model-trees-*, osv-reports/, docs/campaigns/.
/security-review-*.md
/audit-*
/FPR-overnight-*
/fp-analysis-*
/livraison-*
/npm-reports-*
/strategic-positioning-*
scripts/append-*
scripts/auto-*
